{q:"What is clustering?",o:["Grouping similar data points without predefined class labels","Predicting a known numerical target","Sorting records by date","Removing all duplicate rows"],a:0,e:"Clustering is an unsupervised learning task that groups observations based on similarity."},
{q:"Which algorithm is commonly used for clustering?",o:["K-means","Linear regression","Logistic regression","Naive Bayes classifier"],a:0,e:"K-means partitions observations into K clusters by iteratively updating cluster assignments and centroids."},
{q:"What does the K in K-nearest neighbours represent?",o:["Number of nearest training examples considered","Number of output classes only","Number of model epochs","Number of missing values"],a:0,e:"K specifies how many nearby training observations are used to make a prediction."},
{q:"What is the purpose of a training dataset?",o:["Fit the model parameters or learn patterns","Only report the final accuracy","Replace the test dataset","Store the source code"],a:0,e:"The training dataset is used by the learning algorithm to fit the model."},
{q:"Why is a test dataset kept separate from training data?",o:["To estimate performance on unseen examples","To increase the training accuracy","To tune every parameter repeatedly","To remove the need for evaluation"],a:0,e:"A separate test set provides an estimate of how well the model generalizes to unseen data."},
{q:"What is overfitting?",o:["Learning training-specific noise and performing poorly on unseen data","Performing poorly on both training and test data only","Using too few features in every case","Training a model without labels"],a:0,e:"Overfitting occurs when a model fits training details too closely and fails to generalize."},
{q:"What is underfitting?",o:["A model is too simple to capture important patterns in the data","A model memorizes training noise","A test set is larger than training data","A model has too many parameters in every case"],a:0,e:"Underfitting occurs when the model cannot represent the underlying pattern, often performing poorly on training and test data."},
{q:"Which metric is calculated as correct predictions divided by total predictions?",o:["Precision","Recall","Accuracy","F1-score"],a:2,e:"Accuracy is the proportion of all predictions that are correct."},
{q:"Precision is calculated as:",o:["TP / (TP + FP)","TP / (TP + FN)","TN / (TN + FP)","(TP + TN) / total"],a:0,e:"Precision measures the fraction of predicted positive cases that are actually positive."},
{q:"Recall is calculated as:",o:["TP / (TP + FP)","TP / (TP + FN)","TN / (TN + FN)","FP / (FP + TN)"],a:1,e:"Recall measures the fraction of actual positive cases that the model correctly identifies."},
{q:"What is the F1-score?",o:["The harmonic mean of precision and recall","The arithmetic mean of all feature values","The percentage of missing records","The square root of accuracy"],a:0,e:"F1-score combines precision and recall using their harmonic mean: 2PR/(P+R)."},
{q:"Why is feature scaling often important for K-nearest neighbours?",o:["Distance calculations can be dominated by features with larger numeric ranges","It converts classification into regression","It removes the need for training data","It guarantees 100% accuracy"],a:0,e:"KNN uses distances, so features with large scales can dominate unless features are scaled appropriately."},
{q:"What is cross-validation used for?",o:["Assess model performance across multiple data splits","Encrypt the training dataset","Convert labels into features","Replace all preprocessing"],a:0,e:"Cross-validation evaluates a model over multiple train-validation splits to provide a more robust performance estimate."},
{q:"What is data leakage in machine learning?",o:["Information unavailable at prediction time improperly enters model training or evaluation","A model uses a training set","A dataset contains numeric values","A model is saved to disk"],a:0,e:"Data leakage gives the model access to information it would not legitimately have when making real predictions, producing misleading evaluation results."},
{q:"Which Python library provides common machine learning estimators and preprocessing tools?",o:["scikit-learn","Flask","BeautifulSoup","Pygame"],a:0,e:"scikit-learn provides tools for classification, regression, clustering, preprocessing and model evaluation."},
{q:"What is the purpose of a confusion matrix in classification?",o:["Summarize actual versus predicted class counts","Show only the model's training time","Display feature names alphabetically","Calculate the mean of input columns"],a:0,e:"A confusion matrix compares actual and predicted classes, showing true positives, false positives, true negatives and false negatives."}
